  "verbalization": "Luspatercept is associated with Dominant Beta-thalassemia through a chain of indications that link it to Deferasirox, which in turn is linked to the condition. The evidence suggests that Luspatercept may be repurposed for use in patients with Dominant Beta-thalassemia, as it is indicated for Beta-thalassemia Intermedia, Hbb/lcrb, and And Related Diseases, all of which are subtypes of Beta-thalassemia. This implies that Luspatercept may exert a therapeutic effect on the disease through a mechanism that is not yet fully understood, potentially involving the modulation of beta-globin synthesis or other cellular processes. The indirect pathway through Deferasirox, a known treatment for Beta-thalassemia, suggests a possible overlap in therapeutic targets or mechanisms between Luspatercept and Deferasirox. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Luspatercept to be considered a candidate for repurposing in the treatment of Dominant Beta-thalassemia, though further investigation is needed to elucidate the precise mechanism of action.",
